  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "26ae08c47dd1555727664f60f3fe718eb8679cbf",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2590048231,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "There is is a comment and find in: https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/epan/plugin_if.c#L73-74\n\n```c\n    /* For now, a protocol may only register one main menu */\n    ws_assert(g_list_find(menubar_menunames, name) == NULL);\n```\n\nThat does not actually do anything, because it's not comparing the name, it's comparing the *pointer* of the string. (It would need to be `g_list_find_custom(menubar_menunames, name, (GCompareFunc)g_strcmp0) == NULL);` to work as intended, I believe.)\n\nSo at least the original intent by @rknall was to only allow plugins to register one main menu. It's possible that the unique names were only necessary for GTK (there's some comments to the effect in the code), so maybe all of that could be removed.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-06-27T12:17:14.748Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-06-27T13:35:02.959Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 393613805,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2025-06-27T13:35:02.959Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20337,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2590120361,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "That's a very good point and I will definitely test it and modify the patch! I was actually curious why I could register multiple items in the main menu despite that comment and ws_assert. You clarified it: the function was not used correctly. :smile:",
          "author": {
            "id": 20971927,
            "username": "rtommy",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Tamas Regos",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/20971927/avatar.png?v=1788090511",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rtommy"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-06-27T12:41:52.807Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-06-27T13:35:02.959Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 393613805,
