    },
    {
      "id": "378b39b9ddba7b56f197e90273c99591e97aecf7",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2590076473,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Note that as done originally, even if different labels were chosen for the same protocol, the internally generated name would be the same. We might be able to eliminate the internal name and just use the label.\n\nIn that case, we could either disallow multiple entries with the same label, or allow adding them. Allowing them would probably make it impossible to later remove them using the name, but I suppose that is fine. Unlike GTK, Qt *does* allow adding multiple menus with the same name, so this might work.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-06-27T12:27:05.983Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-06-27T12:27:05.983Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 393613805,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 20337,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "2cd8b25f52fd2b3e143129e75efeb987e463a39f",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2590132573,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Yes, I have also realized that internally generated name in the code. Indeed, feels a bit redundant. Note, using different protocols but always the same label ends up with same outcome as this issue I raised. So I agree that the label could be actually checked and validate it to be unique. Allowing the same label multiple time does not seem to be right to me, or at least I cannot think of any real use case or example to support it.\n\nAbove these, overall the improvement is worth merging?",
          "author": {
            "id": 20971927,
            "username": "rtommy",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Tamas Regos",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/20971927/avatar.png?v=1788090511",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rtommy"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-06-27T12:46:25.960Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-06-27T12:46:25.960Z",
